+/* An NSCursor holds one X cursor (its cid).  With monitors of different
+ * scale factors the pointer must change size when it moves to another
+ * monitor, also inside one window (Workspace's desktop spans all monitors),
+ * so each cid remembers what it was made from and gets a sibling X cursor per
+ * factor on demand.  A factor is keyed in hundredths; key 0 means every
+ * monitor runs at 1.0, where cursors are made exactly as before. */
